ℹ Indexing with `x[i]` panics if `i` is out of bounds. When you're not sure the index is valid, use `x.get(i)` — it returns an Option you can handle.
ℹ VB converts between number types silently; Rust wants it spelled out, so Bust inserts `as` for you. A narrowing conversion (e.g. Long → Integer, or a float to an integer) can lose data.
✘ [line 6] `Parallel For` iterations can't all write `total` — that's a race. Each iteration may write a different slot (`arr[i] = …`). A reduction (`total = total + …`) wants `Parallel Sum xs`, not a shared scalar.